The key methods are `getSublistValue` to read and `setSublistValue` to write in standard mode, or `getCurrentSublistValue`/`setCurrentSublistValue` in dynamic mode. The sublist you want on a sales order is `'item'`.

Standard mode example (simplest for server-side scripts):

```javascript
var so = record.load({ type: record.Type.SALES_ORDER, id: 123 });

var lineCount = so.getLineCount({ sublistId: 'item' });

for (var i = 0; i < lineCount; i++) {
    var itemId = so.getSublistValue({ sublistId: 'item', fieldId: 'item', line: i });
    var qty    = so.getSublistValue({ sublistId: 'item', fieldId: 'quantity', line: i });

    // set a value
    so.setSublistValue({ sublistId: 'item', fieldId: 'quantity', line: i, value: 10 });
}

so.save();
```

In dynamic mode (required for client scripts running in the browser) you select the line first, then commit it:

```javascript
so.selectLine({ sublistId: 'item', line: i });
so.setCurrentSublistValue({ sublistId: 'item', fieldId: 'quantity', value: 10 });
so.commitLine({ sublistId: 'item' });
```

The main gotcha: in dynamic mode you MUST call `commitLine` or your changes are silently lost. Also, line indexes are zero-based. Common item sublist field IDs are `item`, `quantity`, `rate`, `amount`, `description`, `taxcode`, `department`, `location`. Want a full list of the item sublist fields?
